Chapter: SlugSuffix
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `slug-has-suffix` in ChapterScoper decides whether a chapter slug ends with
 `--<bare name>`, and it is the hottest comparison in cite resolution: it runs
 per assignment, per citation that misses the composed key, per slug transition
 of the defs walk, in all four passes.

 IT MUST NOT ALLOCATE, which is why it was written as a character loop in the
 first place -- the chapter's own note records that a `substring` form put
 5.4 MB per bare-name citation on the LOWER deck, about 135 MB of the
 selfhost's 302. A `text-contains` guard in front of the loop keeps that
 property (`bs-alloc = "none"`) and rejects the common case in one call
 instead of one call per character.

 THE GUARD IS A FILTER AND NOT THE ANSWER. `text-contains` is implied by
 ending-with and does not imply it: `Foo--Bar--Baz` contains `--Bar` and does
 not end with it. That pair is the reason this file exists.

We say:

Section: The Two Forms

 The loop as it stands.

  old-suffix-eq : Text, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  old-suffix-eq (s) (suf) (base) (j) (fl) =
   if j == fl then True
   else if char-code-at s (base + j) == char-code-at suf j then old-suffix-eq s suf base (j + 1) fl
   else False

  old-has-suffix : Text, Text -> Boolean
  old-has-suffix (s) (suf) =
   let sl = text-length s
   in let fl = text-length suf
   in if fl > sl then False else old-suffix-eq s suf (sl - fl) 0 fl

 The loop with the guard in front of it.

  new-has-suffix : Text, Text -> Boolean
  new-has-suffix (s) (suf) =
   let sl = text-length s
   in let fl = text-length suf
   in if fl > sl then False
      else if text-contains s suf == False then False
      else old-suffix-eq s suf (sl - fl) 0 fl

Section: The Pairs

 Every pair a slug walk can present, and the two that discriminate: a suffix
 that occurs only in the MIDDLE, and one that occurs twice.

  slugs : List Text
  slugs = ["Parsmi--Unification", "Parsmi--Unification", "Foo--Bar--Baz", "Foo--Bar--Baz",
           "Bar", "Bar", "Codex_Codex", "A--B--B", "x", "", "Parsmi--Unify"]

  sufs : List Text
  sufs = ["--Unification", "--Unify", "--Baz", "--Bar",
          "Bar", "--Bar", "--Codex", "--B", "--x", "", "--Unification"]

  want : List Boolean
  want = [True, False, True, False,
          True, False, False, True, False, True, False]

Section: The Check

  check : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  check (i) (n) (bad) =
   if i >= n then bad
   else let s = list-at slugs i
   in let f = list-at sufs i
   in let o = old-has-suffix s f
   in let w = new-has-suffix s f
   in let expected = list-at want i
   in check (i + 1) n (bad + (if o == w & o == expected then 0 else 1))

  report : Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  report (i) (n) (acc) =
   if i >= n then acc
   else let s = list-at slugs i
   in let f = list-at sufs i
   in let line = "\n  " & s & " ends-with " & f & " old=" & show (old-has-suffix s f) & " new=" & show (new-has-suffix s f) & " want=" & show (list-at want i)
   in report (i + 1) n (acc & line)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let n = list-length slugs
    in let bad = check 0 n 0
    in let head = if bad == 0 then "slug-suffix: " & show n & " pairs agree" else "slug-suffix: " & show bad & " of " & show n & " WRONG"
    in print-line-uni (head & report 0 n "")
  end
